From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:57:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 65/86] Clone to other view mirrors the document

Tabs of the same file now hold the same text: an edit in one is applied to
the others right after it, as one change of their own over the range that
differs. Each tab keeps its own cursor, scroll and undo history; undo in
one mirrors like any edit. Saving one marks the others saved, and undoing
back to the saved text does too. Closing one leaves the other a normal tab.

cosmic-text keeps buffer, cursor and undo together in one editor per tab,
so the tabs cannot share a buffer. A mirrored change makes the texts equal,
so it is never mirrored back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

